# Regularization Strategies Comparison Report

## Overview
Comparison of three general-purpose regularization methods for $K x = y$:
1. **Method A (Tikhonov Regularization):** Smooth spectral filtering with L-curve corner selection.
2. **Method B (Truncated SVD / TSVD):** Sharp spectral truncation at the discrepancy/effective rank threshold.
3. **Method C (Conjugate Gradient for Least Squares / CGLS):** Iterative regularization with discrepancy early stopping.

## Performance Summary

| Method | Parameter | Parameter Criterion | Residual Norm ||r|| | Solution Norm ||x|| |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Method A (Tikhonov)** | alpha = 1.337373e-01 | L-curve maximum curvature | 0.4753 | 2.6973 |
| **Method B (TSVD)** | k = 22 | Morozov discrepancy / rank | 0.4191 | 5.0213 |
